  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UN Water - Accelerating progress on SDG 6</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The main objective of the present proposal is the acceleration of SDG 6 progress as an essential contribution to the successful implementation of the water-related 2030 Agenda targets and the Water Action Decade. To this end, UN-Water continues to operationalize the SDG 6 Global Acceleration Framework as an overarching approach to strengthen the global water architecture and to ensure availability and sustainable management of water and sanitation for all. The SDG 6 Global Acceleration Framework mobilizes action through focusing the attention of Member States, United Nations entities and other stakeholders specifically on five cross-cutting `accelerators&#xbf; &#xbf; Financing, Data &amp; Information, Capacity Development, Innovation, and Governance &#xbf; in order to drive progress on water and sanitation issues. The specific objectives include:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;ordered&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;Enhance the capacities and overall coherence of the UN system for effective and coherent multilateral water governance and country coordination&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;ordered&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Enhance international, regional, and national policy dialogues on the acceleration of SDG 6 implementation and water-related Goals of the 2030 Agenda&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;ordered&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;Strengthen integrated monitoring, reporting and use of data by countries for the achievement of SDG 6.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;ordered&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Strengthen country level engagement in support of the UN reform and the SDG 6 Global Acceleration Framework.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
